1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:03,439
Hi everyone. Today I'm going to walk you

2
00:00:03,439 --> 00:00:05,200
through how to schedule task reminders

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,680
in Blitzet. A simple but an effective

4
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,599
way to keep your tasks on track and

5
00:00:09,599 --> 00:00:12,800
never miss an important deadline. So to

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,679
schedule a reminder, hover over a task,

7
00:00:15,679 --> 00:00:18,000
open the expanded menu, and click

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,240
schedule. This opens a scheduleuling

9
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:22,800
popup, your command panel foruling your

10
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,400
reminders.

11
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,640
In the popup, you can choose a specific

12
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:29,599
date and time for your reminder. Blitzet

13
00:00:29,599 --> 00:00:31,279
also offers quick shortcuts for date

14
00:00:31,279 --> 00:00:33,200
selections to help you pick a feeding

15
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,120
option fast.

16
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:37,760
Today is today's date. Later today sets

17
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:39,440
the reminder for two hours ahead of your

18
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:41,680
current time. Tomorrow's picks

19
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,000
tomorrow's date and next week schedule

20
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,440
the reminder exactly 7 days from today.

21
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,520
So yeah, just select the date that works

22
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:51,840
best for you. Then hit next to go to the

23
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,399
time selection screen. Here you can

24
00:00:54,399 --> 00:00:56,320
click the add button to specify an exact

25
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:58,559
time for your reminder.

26
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:00,640
If you don't set a specific time, the

27
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,239
task will automatically move to the due

28
00:01:02,239 --> 00:01:06,320
today column on its due date.

29
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,960
Let's also supports recurring schedules.

30
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,880
Recurring tasks create a parent task in

31
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,640
your backlog which automatically

32
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,640
generates individual child tasks each

33
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:17,360
week. These child tasks are pretty much

34
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,119
regular tasks you can manage and

35
00:01:19,119 --> 00:01:21,280
complete independently.

36
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,200
In the schedule popup, you can set

37
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:25,119
different intervals.

38
00:01:25,119 --> 00:01:27,280
Every day it creates seven new child

39
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,320
tasks every Monday, one for each day.

40
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,799
Every weekday, this one creates five new

41
00:01:32,799 --> 00:01:35,040
child tasks every Monday for Monday to

42
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:37,840
Friday. Every specific day, the tasks

43
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,600
repeat on the same weekday you picked in

44
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,920
the date section, like every Saturday in

45
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:45,119
this case. Every month, task repeat

46
00:01:45,119 --> 00:01:47,520
monthly on the date you chose. This is

47
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,439
perfect for routine tasks like weekly

48
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:52,399
reports or monthly check-ins. For a

49
00:01:52,399 --> 00:01:53,840
detailed look at how the recurrent

50
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,840
schedules feature works, check out our

51
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,479
tutorial on recurrent schedules. Once

52
00:01:58,479 --> 00:02:00,399
you're done, click schedule to save your

53
00:02:00,399 --> 00:02:03,280
reminder. Once saved, your schedule

54
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:05,360
tasks will appear in one of the columns

55
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:08,000
depending on the reminder date. This

56
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,599
way, you get a clear view of what's

57
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:11,039
coming up and can plan your day

58
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:13,120
accordingly.

59
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:15,120
If your plans change, you can easily

60
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:17,040
edit a scheduled reminder by opening the

61
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,599
tasks expanded menu and clicking update

62
00:02:19,599 --> 00:02:21,440
schedule. Then you can adjust the

63
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:23,040
parameters.

64
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:25,360
To remove a scheduled reminder, simply

65
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:27,200
click the X icon next to the schedule

66
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,480
details. The task itself stays intact.

67
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:33,280
Only the reminder is removed.

68
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,040
Sheduling reminders in Blitzet helps you

69
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,640
stay ahead of your tasks without the

70
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:39,599
usual oops, I forgot moments. Try it out

71
00:02:39,599 --> 00:02:42,080
and see how much easier your days got.

72
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:44,080
If you found this tutorial helpful,

73
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,599
don't forget to check out our other

74
00:02:45,599 --> 00:02:47,519
videos and join our Discord community

75
00:02:47,519 --> 00:02:49,840
for more tips and support. Happy

76
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,380
blitzing.

77
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:54,490
[Music]